---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { capabilityState } from "../utilities/public-capabilities";

const explorer = capabilityState("explorer");
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Enterprise Reality"
  description="Understand the enterprise beyond its systems, and why coherent governed understanding matters."
  canonicalPath="/"
>
  <section class="page-hero section">
    <div class="container page-hero__inner">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Enterprise Reality</p>
        <h1>The enterprise exists beyond its systems</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          An enterprise is made of people, places, obligations, events,
          decisions and consequences. Its systems record parts of that reality;
          none necessarily holds the whole picture.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" aria-labelledby="fragmentation">
    <div class="container content-grid">
      <div class="content-grid__context">
        <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="fragmentation">Understanding becomes fragmented</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Records, observations and decisions accumulate in operational systems
          built for different purposes. The result can be a fragmented account
          of what is happening, why it is believed, and what should be
          considered next.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="supporting-note">
        <strong>One situation.</strong><br />Several legitimate observations.
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="damp-mould">
    <div class="container content-grid">
      <div class="content-grid__context">
        <p class="eyebrow">A concrete situation</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="damp-mould">Damp &amp; Mould makes the problem visible</h2>
        <p>
          A resident report, property history, inspection observations, repair
          records and policy may each sit in a different place. The question is
          not simply where the data is; it is how the enterprise can understand
          the situation coherently while preserving what is uncertain or
          disputed.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/case-studies/damp-and-mould/"
            >Follow the Damp &amp; Mould case</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul
        class="relationship relationship--observations"
        aria-label="Illustrative distributed observations"
      >
        <li>Resident report</li><li>Inspection observation</li><li>
          Repair record
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" aria-labelledby="missing-capability">
    <div class="container content-grid">
      <div class="content-grid__context">
        <p class="eyebrow">What is missing</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="missing-capability">Coherent governed understanding</h2>
        <p class="proposition">
          What is missing is not another copy of the data.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="supporting-note">
        A governed way to connect identity, relationships, events, evidence and
        provenance without pretending that disagreement or incomplete
        observation has disappeared.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="enterprise-reality">
    <div class="container content-grid">
      <div class="content-grid__context">
        <p class="eyebrow">The response</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="enterprise-reality">Enterprise Reality</h2>
        <p>
          Enterprise Reality is the governed representation through which an
          enterprise can understand what its evidence justifies. It does not
          replace the enterprise, its people or its operational systems.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/enterprise-reality/">Understand Enterprise Reality</a></p>
      </div>
      <p class="supporting-note">
        Understanding connects the enterprise whole while preserving the
        boundaries of its systems.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" aria-labelledby="platform">
    <div class="container reading-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">From understanding to execution</p>
      <h2 id="platform">The Platform makes Enterprise Reality executable</h2>
      <p>
        The Platform provides the bounded technical capabilities through which
        governed representations can be worked with. It is not the opening
        proposition: execution follows understanding.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/platform/">Explore the current Platform overview</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="explorer">
    <div class="container content-grid">
      <div class="content-grid__context">
        <p class="eyebrow">Human experience</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="explorer">
          Explorer helps people investigate Enterprise Reality
        </h2>
        <p>
          Explorer is an authorised product with implemented and demonstrated
          programme capability. Its public commercial availability is not
          claimed.
        </p>
        <p><a href="/explorer/">Understand the Explorer experience</a></p>
      </div>
      <aside class="authority-note">
        Programme standing: {explorer.programmeStanding}. Capability maturity: {
          explorer.maturity
        }.
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" aria-labelledby="downstream">
    <div class="container reading-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">What follows</p>
      <h2 id="downstream">
        Reasoning and action are downstream of understanding
      </h2>
      <p>
        Reasoning can assess governed relationships and evidence. Decisions,
        authorised action, automation and AI remain bounded downstream
        responsibilities; none replaces the need to understand the situation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="verification">
    <div class="container reading-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">Verification</p>
      <h2 id="verification">Reference substantiates understanding</h2>
      <p>
        Deeper programme authority and approved public evidence remain available
        for verification. They support the explanation; they do not have to
        precede it.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/knowledge/">Explore the public record</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style></style>
